1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:10,700
Two eighteen-metre cat-ladders — engineered vertical access for a Buroh Street warehouse and its adjoining repair facility.

2
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:16,620
Built from high-strength aluminium alloy. Lightweight, corrosion-resistant, built to perform.

3
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:22,330
Each ladder is enclosed in a full safety cage — assembled rung by rung, to specification.

4
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:27,540
A mid-height landing platform breaks the climb — a code-compliant rest point on the ascent.

5
00:00:27,590 --> 00:00:35,220
Installation was executed from a boom-lift under full fall-arrest protocol — every worker harnessed.

6
00:00:35,270 --> 00:00:39,990
A vertical access system is only as safe as its anchor.

7
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:44,770
So we anchored it with galvanised mild-steel brackets and Fischer M16 anchor bolts.

8
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:48,990
Every anchor is proof-load tested on site — a Fischer pull-out test.

9
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:53,640
Documented and verified before handover. We don't assume. We verify.

10
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:56,340
Lockable gates at the base secure the access.

11
00:00:56,390 --> 00:01:03,690
Two eighteen-metre runs — Professional Engineer-certified, load-calculated, built to perform.

12
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:12,500
Ezzogenics. Custom-engineered. Anchored. Certified.  metalsingapore.sg  |  metalglassworksingapore.com

